    "humanReview": "Qualitative user feedback recorded; revised finish awaits another human review. No user scores assigned.",
    "solution": "Save an echo on the isolated upper perch, then take the lower ledge to the ring. Extend the far arc for the low tally, haul in and steer through the return. As the swing starts rising to the right, jump-release and swap during the rise; simultaneous Jump + Echo is also valid. The wider, lower receiving shelf catches a range of successful launches. Simply returning to stand on the echo perch still leaves an ordinary jump short of the far shelf.",
    "nearestExisting": "p131 The Citadel and F19 The Weight Must Stay relocate a prepared machinery launch. Here the launch is made by changing a rope length and steering a pendulum after a low objective; the direction and vertical component at release determine whether the relocated arc clears the gulf.",
    "novelty": "There is no dash fallback. The low tally asks for an extended outward arc; the exit asks for a shortened rising return. The same controllable pendulum must supply both trajectories, and the echo transports its velocity across an otherwise lethal beam partition. The upper route is deliberately beyond an ordinary jump from the echo perch.",
    "designNotes": "Geometry-only revision. The canonical preview uses a three-frame gap between jump-release and echo; simultaneous inputs also work. Normal-spawn tolerance checks vary both the release timing and swap delay, rather than proving only one exact tape. No attached-rope teleport or new input rules.",
